// StdToArm64Conversion — arm64 instruction selection: Std → the unified `TargetOp`'s arm64 band.
//
// ⭐ WAVE-1 STUB (arm64-macOS foundation rung). This rung landed the CONTRACT — the arm64 `TargetOp`
// arms, their operand model, their printing, the neutral register model and the ABI pools — and
// wired the backend so an `arm64-macos` build REACHES here. The isel itself is wave 1.
//
// The counterpart of `StdToX64Conversion.lowerStdToX64`, and it returns the SAME pair — a
// `TargetModule` plus the per-function `ValueClassColumns` — because the class column crosses the
// tier boundary here, at the last pass that can see a Std type (see BackendDispatch.buildBackend and
// TargetDialect's `ValueClassColumn`). Wave 1 emits the arm64 band: 3-address ALU with plain defs
// (no two-address reuse), `movz`/`movk` const materialization, the ADRP+ADD address pairs, the
// explicit divide-by-zero guard arm64 needs (its `sdiv` does not trap — M1 divergence note), the
// NaN-safe float compares (`flt`→`mi`, `fle`→`ls`), and the macOS lowering of `osAlloc`/`osWrite`
// through libSystem. Reg-reg moves, spills and base+disp loads reuse the shared neutral ops.
export function lowerStdToArm64(stdModule StdModule, globalData GlobalDataTable) returns (TargetModule, ValueClassColumns)
	panic("arm64 lowerStdToArm64: not yet implemented (wave 1) [{stdModule.funcCount()} fn, {globalData.dataSection.count()} data]")
end 'lowerStdToArm64'
